--TEST--
A `secret` value in a `<?= … ?>` hole of an html template is refused where it is written, exactly as in a `{$…}` hole — `rule:security/secret-sinks-refuse`, ADR 0202
--FILE--
<?nvs
secret string $token = "hunter2";
echo html`<p><?= $token ?></p>`;
--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0790]: an `html` template cannot print a `secret` value
  --> %s:3:18
  |
3 | echo html`<p><?= $token ?></p>`;
  |                  ^^^^^^ this value is `secret`
  = help: Output is read by people and saved in logs. To print the value anyway, call `Core\Secret::reveal($value, "reason")` first. Joining it into a longer string does not help. The result is `secret` too.

